# Audit evidence records live here, and for them the captured stdout/stderr IS
# the evidence: the build log carrying the warning policy, the signature and
# axiom-cone log, the per-checkout identity logs.
#
# The repository-wide `*.log` rule (/.gitignore line 9) is right for build
# scratch and wrong here.  Without this exception `git add` silently skips
# exactly the load-bearing artifacts and leaves a manifest that lists files the
# commit does not contain -- an evidence record that cannot be verified from
# the repository is not an evidence record.
!*.log
